{
  "_comment": [
    "Codex hook configuration. agentkit writes this into the repo's .codex/hooks.json.",
    "",
    "TRUST CAVEAT, and it is the reason this file is not the safety story on its own:",
    "hooks discovered from the PROJECT layer and the USER layer (~/.codex/hooks.json) are",
    "both non-managed, which means they carry Codex's hash-trust requirement and are",
    "disableable. The design's earlier claim that the user layer was trust-independent was",
    "refuted against the shipped source at rust-v0.147.0: ConfigLayerSource::User maps to",
    "is_managed = false, exactly like the project layer.",
    "",
    "The trust-FREE layer is the SYSTEM layer: /etc/codex/config.toml with an inline",
    "[hooks] table, which is is_managed = true and cannot be disabled. It needs one sudo,",
    "no MDM and no paid plan. That is Tier 0b in the design, and it is the layer to use for",
    "anything that must hold regardless of what the workspace says.",
    "",
    "Also measured: Codex's trust hash covers the config-derived hook IDENTITY, never the",
    "invoked script's bytes. Editing a gate script costs zero re-trust and produces zero",
    "signal. Do not treat the hash as tamper-evidence for the script itself."
  ],
  "hooks": {
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Bash",
        "command": ["${CODEX_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/agentkit/pretooluse-bash.sh"]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "apply_patch",
        "command": ["${CODEX_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/agentkit/pretooluse-write.py"]
      }
    ]
  }
}
